# An allow-list, not a deny-list.
#
# A deny-list is one forgotten line away from baking a developer's SQLite
# database, a local `.env`, or a checkout of somebody else's source tree into a
# published image. Everything is excluded and the four things the build needs
# are named, so a new directory in this repository cannot silently join them.
*

!pyproject.toml
!painfree/
!deploy/requirements.lock
!deploy/requirements-build.lock

# The wheel the build stage produces carries the readme as its description and
# both licence files in its metadata, so the build fails without these three.
# That is the correct failure: an image whose wheel has dropped the MIT notice
# it is obliged to keep is not one to ship.
!README.md
!LICENSE
!NOTICE

# Nothing compiled on the host belongs in the image: it is built for whatever
# Python the developer happened to have.
painfree/**/__pycache__/
painfree/**/*.pyc
